    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=acafb953-757f-4fc8-b0ee-c3d3b317c413&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9202897053373_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\n\nLocation: Macon\n\nWesleyan College is seeking an experienced instructor to teach introductory Chemistry courses. Wesleyan College, a four-year national liberal arts college for women, is located in Macon, Georgia, 70 miles south of Atlanta. Wesleyan was the first college in the world chartered to grant degrees to women. Wesleyan’s academically challenging, inclusive environment helps prepare students to live purposeful and connected lives. Strengths of this small liberal arts college are our diverse student population and our commitment to liberal arts throughout our curriculum.  This is a part-time adjunct position. To apply, upload a cover letter, resumé including three professional references, brief teaching philosophy, and an unofficial transcript from the institution(s) where relevant graduate work was completed.  Applications lacking the required documents will not be considered.  Applications will be considered until the position is filled.  Duties and Responsibilities: Teach course(s) conforming to departmental and institutional standards and expectations Communicate and uphold clear, consistent student learning outcomes, grading policies, and e-mail/message response practices throughout the term Maintain a student-friendly, ADA accessible, and up-to-date Canvas LMS course site  Evaluate student achievement of specified learning outcomes and assign grades Post four-week, midterm, and final student grades according to College-specified deadlines Respond to student questions and learning needs in a respectful, compassionate, and timely manner Stay current regarding the professional body of knowledge in the field of practice Complete required administrative tasks according to College-specified deadlines, including: completing all hiring paperwork; signing instructor contract; submitting updated syllabus;  posting attendance, grade, and student concern reports; and reporting institutional learning outcome data Other duties as assigned Qualifications and Experience: Candidate must have a Master's or doctoral degree in Chemistry from a regionally accredited institution. Candidate should have a minimum of two years of college-level teaching experience. Candidate should have experience designing and maintaining an LMS course site.  Candidate will be required to submit copies of official transcripts (all degree levels) upon hire. Wesleyan College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The College supports equal employment opportunities for all persons without regard to race, color, creed, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, gender, national origin, status as a war veteran, age, disability, or any other status protected by law. Wesleyan College is a certified drug-free workplace employer. All applicants being considered for employment are required to submit to substance screening as a condition of employment.   Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the United States, individuals will be required to provide proof of identity and eligibility for employment in the United States upon acceptance of an employment offer. In addition, employment is contingent upon successfully passing a criminal background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=acafb953-757f-4fc8-b0ee-c3d3b317c413&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9202893254115_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Basketball",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\n\nLocation: Macon\n\nAssistant Coach, Basketball Wesleyan College, a member of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and the Southern States Athletic Conference (SSAC), seeks qualified candidates for an Assistant Coach / Player Development Coach for Women's Basketball.  The Assistant Coach / Player Development Coach will assist the Head Women's Basketball Coach in carrying out the objectives of the athletics program as outlined by the Head Coach and Director of Athletics. The primary responsibility of this position will be the development of student-athletes through individual skill development, basketball fundamentals, game preparation, and team strategies. The Assistant Coach / Player Development Coach will also play a significant role in the recruitment and retention of student-athletes and will assist with the planning and coordination of team travel and itineraries.  This position reports directly to the Head Women's Basketball Coach in conjunction with the Director of Athletics. The successful candidate will be expected to know and/or quickly familiarize themselves with and adhere to all NAIA, SSAC, and Wesleyan College rules, regulations, and policies.  Pay for this position is a $2,500 stipend paid monthly over the course of the basketball season.  Essential Duties:  Assist the Head Coach in planning and conducting practices, workouts, individual skill-development sessions, and team activities.  Serve as a primary resource for individual player development, including fundamental skills, position-specific development, basketball IQ, decision-making, and overall performance. Develop and implement individual player development plans in collaboration with the Head Coach.  Assist in preparing student-athletes for competition through film study, scouting, game preparation, and implementation of team and individual strategies.  Assist with coaching during practices, games, and other team activities.  Assist the Head Coach with the recruitment of prospective student-athletes in accordance with NAIA, SSAC, and Wesleyan College rules and regulations.  Identify, evaluate, communicate with, and build relationships with prospective student-athletes and their families.  Assist with recruiting visits, campus visits, prospect evaluations, recruiting events, and other recruiting activities as assigned by the Head Coach.  Assist in maintaining positive and professional relationships with prospective student-athletes, current student-athletes, families, high school coaches, club coaches, and other recruiting contacts.  Coordinate team travel logistics in conjunction with the Head Coach and appropriate College personnel.  Develop and maintain team travel itineraries, including transportation, lodging, meals, departure times, arrival times, game schedules, and other necessary travel information.  Communicate travel itineraries and updates effectively to student-athletes, coaches, and appropriate College personnel.  Assist with team travel, including transportation, lodging, meals, game-day logistics, and other responsibilities associated with team competition.  Adhere to and support the academic standards and requirements of Wesleyan College regarding the eligibility and academic progress of student-athletes.  Assist student-athletes by providing appropriate advice and assistance to support their academic, athletic, and personal development.  Monitor and encourage student-athlete accountability, preparation, discipline, and commitment to team expectations.  Report any known or suspected violations of Wesleyan College, NAIA, or SSAC rules and regulations to the Head Coach and/or Director of Athletics.  Assist with administrative responsibilities related to the women's basketball program as assigned by the Head Coach.  Represent Wesleyan College and the women's basketball program in a professional manner at all times.  Qualifications:  Bachelor's degree preferred.  One or more years of successful high school, college, or professional playing experience is preferred.  Previous collegiate coaching experience preferred, particularly at the NAIA, NCAA, or junior college level.  Demonstrated ability to develop student-athletes' individual basketball skills and overall understanding of the game.  Ability to evaluate talent and assist with the identification and recruitment of prospective student-athletes.  Strong organizational skills with the ability to coordinate team travel and manage detailed itineraries.  Ability to assess a team's competitive strengths and vulnerabilities.  Demonstrated skill in making recommendations to enhance individual and team performance.  Working knowledge of or willingness to learn NAIA and SSAC rules and regulations.  Ability to work a flexible and irregular schedule, including evenings, weekends, holidays, and travel.  Candidates must have:  Proven ability to communicate effectively one-on-one, in small groups, and in a public setting.  Ability to communicate ideas and priorities effectively to promote teamwork and achieve desired results.  Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills.  Creativity, flexibility, humility, maturity, and patience.  Strong organizational and time-management skills.  Commitment to the academic, athletic, and personal development of student-athletes.  Commitment to Wesleyan College's core values.  To apply for this position, upload a letter of interest, resume, and three references, preferably in one PDF document. Applications without the required documents may not be considered. Due to the volume of applicants, we are unable to respond to each applicant individually. Posting may close as soon as an applicant pool is identified.  Wesleyan College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The College supports equal employment opportunities for all persons without regard to race, color, creed, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, gender, national origin, status as a war veteran, age, disability, or any other status protected by law. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the United States. Individuals will be required to provide proof of identity and eligibility for employment in the United States upon acceptance of an employment offer.  Wesleyan College is a certified drug-free workplace employer. All applicants being considered for employment are required to submit to substance screening and must pass a criminal background check as a condition of employment.",
